<title>USA: Wheelabrator Q4 oper loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Wheelabrator Q4 oper loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>HAMPTON, N.H. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr loss	    $0.11   profit	 $0.06</p>
<p> Oper net loss	   17,912   profit	10,899</p>
<p> Revs		     245,723		  226,838</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 162,000		  182,500</p>
<p>NOTE: Operating earnings are from continuing operations.  </p>
<p>1996 Q4 net loss was $131.9 million or $0.81 a share, after including a gain of $1.1 million or $0.01 a share from discontinued operations and a loss of $115.1 million or $0.71 a share from Rust unit's discontinued operations.</p>
<p>1995 Q4 net loss was $10.2 million or $0.06 a share after including a gain of $6.2 million or $0.03 a share from income from discontinued operations and a loss of $27.3 million or $0.15 a share from Rust discontinued operations.  </p>
<p>		   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	  $0.65   profit	 $0.73</p>
<p> Oper net profit	109,454   profit     134,283</p>
<p> Revs		     952,312		  956,088</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 169,400		  185,000</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
</text>
